 `new_workspace_cwd` accepts the same values as `new_cwd` and applies to workspaces created from the sidebar, the `new_workspace` keybinding, `herdr workspace create` without `--cwd`, and the default workspace Herdr opens when none exist. New panes and tabs keep following `new_cwd`. When unset, workspaces use `new_cwd`. Worktree workspaces always start in their worktree checkout, a server auto-started by `herdr` opens its first workspace in the directory it was launched from, and explicit `--cwd` values still take precedence.
 
+Panes that have not enabled a keyboard protocol receive Shift+Enter as a bare carriage return, the same as Enter. To send the CSI-u sequence `ESC[13;2u` instead, so a shell can bind Shift+Enter separately (for example zsh `bindkey '^[[13;2u' autosuggest-accept`):
+
+```toml
+[terminal]
+shift_enter_csi_u = true
+```
+
+Panes that negotiate kitty keyboard or modifyOtherKeys keep their own Shift+Enter encoding. The setting applies to the next key after a config reload. In remote sessions, the server's setting is used.
+
